{"summary":"The common sandpiper (Actitis hypoleucos) is a small Palearctic wader. This bird and its American sister species, the spotted sandpiper (A. macularia), make up the genus Actitis. They are parapatric and replace each other geographically; stray birds of either species may settle down with breeders of the other and hybridize. Hybridization has also been reported between the common sandpiper and the green sandpiper, a basal species of the closely related shank genus Tringa.","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Actitis hypoleucos","cells":[[-21.6,21.4,1],[-19.0,16.5,1],[-21.6,16.5,1],[-19.6,20.7,1],[-17.0,13.7,1],[-20.3,17.2,1],[-17.6,20.0,1],[-18.3,22.1,2],[-21.0,14.4,1],[-17.6,13.7,1],[-18.3,20.7,1],[-17.6,14.4,1],[-19.0,22.1,1],[-19.0,13.7,1],[-18.3,21.4,2],[-21.0,16.5,1],[-19.0,17.2,1],[-18.3,25.0,1],[-21.6,34.8,1],[-20.3,25.7,1],[-17.6,31.3,1],[-15.6,28.5,1],[-16.3,28.5,1],[-21.0,30.6,1],[-21.0,31.3,1],[-15.6,29.9,1],[-15.6,32.0,1],[-21.0,32.7,1],[-21.6,35.5,1],[-19.0,22.9,1],[-17.0,23.6,1],[-19.0,34.8,1],[-18.3,26.4,1],[-17.6,23.6,1],[-15.6,29.2,2],[-18.3,23.6,1],[-19.6,34.8,1],[-20.3,24.3,1],[-16.3,34.8,2],[-15.6,34.8,2],[-17.6,30.6,2],[-21.6,32.0,1],[-21.0,32.0,1],[-19.0,22.1,1],[-20.3,23.6,1],[-19.0,24.3,1],[-16.3,34.1,1],[-17.6,24.3,2],[-19.0,23.6,2],[-15.6,25.7,1],[-19.6,22.9,1],[-20.3,28.5,1],[-17.0,28.5,1],[-16.3,29.2,1],[-19.0,26.4,1],[-17.0,39.0,1],[-19.6,23.6,2],[-18.3,24.3,1],[-21.6,32.7,1],[-17.6,25.0,3],[-17.6,25.7,3],[-20.3,32.0,1],[-21.6,21.4,1],[-32.8,18.6,1],[-33.4,17.9,1],[-26.7,20.7,1],[-34.0,19.3,1],[-32.2,19.3,1],[-23.6,15.1,1],[-34.0,21.4,1],[-22.3,17.2,2],[-32.8,19.3,1],[-28.6,20.7,1],[-32.8,17.9,2],[-34.0,20.7,1],[-34.6,19.3,2],[-22.9,14.4,2],[-28.0,17.2,1],[-33.4,18.6,2],[-22.9,17.2,1],[-26.7,15.1,1],[-34.6,20.0,2],[-34.6,21.4,1],[-34.0,22.1,2],[-34.0,18.6,2],[-25.5,29.2,1],[-28.0,31.3,1],[-32.2,25.7,1],[-28.0,25.0,1],[-31.7,29.2,1],[-28.6,26.4,1],[-23.6,35.5,1],[-22.3,29.9,1],[-28.6,29.9,1],[-32.8,28.5,2],[-26.7,27.1,1],[-21